    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** providing the clear anchor; his 82.97 score is buoyed by an elite 0.477 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Fedde (4.78 xERA), providing the ceiling we desperately need. **Trea Turner** (68.68) and **Colt Keith** (68.51) follow close behind, both benefiting immensely from the leadoff spot and a high-upside matchup against Avila. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (61.96) is a vital start today; given our organizational focus on stolen bases, his 14% platoon boost against the right-handed Ashcraft makes him an efficient engine for that scarce category. Similarly, **Kyle Schwarber** (65.21) remains a high-floor utility play, leveraging his strong order placement to mitigate any risk from the matchup against Will Warren.\n\nThe rotation strategy continues to prioritize efficiency, leaving **Josh Smith** (38.43) and **Chase Meidroth** (35.33) on the pine as they fell below the Zebras' 40.0 floor. **Josh Smith** was the closest to a start, but his poor BvP history against Gilbert and a suppressed #8 spot in the order kept him benched. While **Casey Schmitt** (54.63) occupies a mid-tier spot, his projection is notably inflated by an 11% platoon advantage and wind conditions favoring a breakout, proving that even our depth pieces are positioned to capitalize on specific environmental edges. We continue to monitor the status of **Christian Yelich** and **Hyeseong Kim**, who remain sidelined, as we rely on the remaining active corps to maintain our category standings.",
